ont-weight:700; color:var(--ink); line-height:1.06; letter-spacing:-0.03em; margin:0 0 18px; text-wrap:balance;">Power modules for electrified vehicles</h1><p style="font-size:16px; color:var(--ink-2); line-height:1.65; margin:0; text-wrap:pretty;">Hana assembles <a href="/markets/power-management/igbt-sic-modules">IGBT and silicon-carbide power modules</a> for traction inverters, on-board chargers and DC-DC converters. Automotive-qualified processes include die attach, silver sintering, wire or clip interconnect and thermal-path control.</p></div><div style="position:relative; overflow:hidden; border-radius:10px; border:1px solid var(--line); background:#fff; aspect-ratio:16/9;"><img src="/images/photos/mk-automotive-power-modules-open-top.webp" alt="Open-top view of an assembled power module showing die attach and interconnect" style="width:100%; height:100%; object-fit:cover; display:block;"/></div></div></div><div style="position:relative; z-index:1; padding:10px 48px; max-width:976px;"><div class="auto-spec"><div class="cell"><div class="l">Qualified</div><div class="v long">AEC-Q101</div></div><div class="cell"><div class="l">Device types</div><div class="v long">IGBT · SiC</div></div><div class="cell"><div class="l">Die attach</div><div class="v long">Ag sinter</div></div><div class="cell"><div class="l">Tested in-house</div><div class="v long">Power cycle</div></div></div></div><div style="position:relative; z-index:1; padding:20px 48px; max-width:976px;"><div class="auto-sechead"><h2>The capability behind power modules</h2><p>Automotive power-module programs draw on Hana's broader microelectronics and OSAT assembly processes.</p></div><div style="border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:var(--radius-card); background:#fff; overflow:hidden;"><div style="padding:28px 30px 24px;"><h3 style="font-family:var(--font-display); font-size:21px; font-weight:600; color:var(--ink); line-height:1.2; letter-spacing:-0.01em; margin:0 0 12px;">Built on Hana's PCBA and micro-assembly lines</h3><p style="font-size:14px; color:var(--ink-2); line-height:1.65; margin:0 0 20px; max-width:560px;">Power-module lines combine Hana's PCBA operations with micro-assembly: die attach, bonding and encapsulation from the microelectronics side, board-level SMT and assembly from the PCBA side. The process route is adapted to the electrical and thermal requirements of the module.</p><div style="display:flex; flex-direction:column; align-items:flex-start; gap:10px;"><a href="/capabilities/microelectronic-assembly" style="font-size:11px; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:0.08em; text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--hana-blue); text-decoration:none; display:inline-flex; align-items:center; gap:6px; white-space:nowrap; line-height:1.4;">See Microelectronic Assembly <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></a><a href="/capabilities/pcba-box-build" style="font-size:11px; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:0.08em; text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--hana-blue); text-decoration:none; display:inline-flex; align-items:center; gap:6px; white-space:nowrap; line-height:1.4;">See PCBA &amp; box build <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></a><a href="/markets/power-management/igbt-sic-modules" style="font-size:11px; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:0.08em; text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--hana-blue); text-decoration:none; display:inline-flex; align-items:center; gap:6px; white-space:nowrap; line-height:1.4;">See IGBT &amp; SiC modules <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></a></div></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--line); padding:22px 30px 26px; display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(3, minmax(0,1fr)); gap:16px;"><figure style="margin:0;"><div style="border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--surface);aspect-ratio:4/3;"><img src="/images/photos/mk-automotive-power-modules-placement.webp" alt="Automated placement head over a wafer on a power module line" style="display:block;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;"/></div><figcaption style="font-size:11px; color:var(--ink-3); line-height:1.5; margin-top:8px;">Die placement</figcaption></figure><figure style="margin:0;"><div style="border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--surface);aspect-ratio:4/3;"><img src="/images/photos/mk-automotive-power-modules-tray.webp" alt="Assembled power modules held in a test fixture tray" style="display:block;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;"/></div><figcaption style="font-size:11px; color:var(--ink-3); line-height:1.5; margin-top:8px;">Fixtured for test</figcaption></figure><figure style="margin:0;"><div style="border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--surface);aspect-ratio:4/3;"><img src="/images/photos/mk-automotive-power-modules-test.webp" alt="Automated module test handler" style="display:block;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;"/></div><figcaption style="font-size:11px; color:var(--ink-3); line-height:1.5; margin-top:8px;">Automated module test</figcaption></figure></div></div></div></div><div style="background:#071f35; border-top:1px solid var(--line); padding:40px 0;"><div style="max-width:976px; padding:0 48px;"><div class="auto-sechead on-dark"><h2>Where it&#39;s made</h2><p>Power-module assembly is supported in Thailand and China, with production focused on automotive and other high-reliability applications.</p></div><div class="auto-plants" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(3, 1fr);"><a class="auto-plantcard" href="/locations/ayutthaya" style="text-decoration:none; color:inherit;"><div><span class="co"><i data-lucide="map-pin" style="width:13px;height:13px;"></i> Thailand</span><div class="nm">Ayutthaya</div></div><span class="cta">View plant <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></span></a><a class="auto-plantcard" href="/locations/jiaxing" style="text-decoration:none; color:inherit;"><div><span class="co"><i data-lucide="map-pin" style="width:13px;height:13px;"></i> China</span><div class="nm">Jiaxing</div></div><span class="cta">View plant <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></span></a><a class="auto-plantcard" href="/locations/lamphun" style="text-decoration:none; color:inherit;"><div><span class="co"><i data-lucide="map-pin" style="width:13px;height:13px;"></i> Thailand</span><div class="nm">Lamphun</div></div><span class="cta">View plant <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></span></a></div><p style="font-size:13px; color:rgba(255,255,255,0.5); line-height:1.5; margin:18px 0 0;"><a href="/locations" style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.75); text-decoration:none; font-weight:600;">View all locations &rarr;</a></p></div></div><div style="background:var(--bg); border-top:1px solid var(--line); padding:40px 0 48px;"><div style="max-width:976px; padding:0 48px;"><div class="auto-sechead"><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2></div><div class="auto-faq"><div class="item is-open"><button type="button" class="q"><span class="num">01</span><h3 class="qt">What power devices can Hana assemble into modules?</h3><span class="chev"><i data-lucide="chevron-down" style="width:16px;height:16px;"></i></span></button><div class="panel"><span></span><p>Hana supports IGBT and silicon-carbide (SiC) die in single- and multi-die layouts, with solder or silver-sinter die attach and aluminum-wire or copper-clip interconnect.</p></div></div><div class="item "><button type="button" class="q"><span class="num">02</span><h3 class="qt">Why does silver sintering matter for SiC?</h3><span class="chev"><i data-lucide="chevron-down" style="width:16px;height:16px;"></i></span></button><div class="panel"><span></span><p>SiC devices operate at higher temperatures and switching speeds than conventional silicon devices. Silver-sinter die attach provides improved thermal and mechanical performance under elevated temperature and repeated thermal cycling.</p></div></div><div class="item "><button type="button" class="q"><span class="num">03</span><h3 class="qt">How is the thermal path controlled?</h3><span class="chev"><i data-lucide="chevron-down" style="width:16px;height:16px;"></i></span></button><div class="panel"><span></span><p>The thermal path is managed through DBC or AMB ceramic substrates, baseplate attachment and controlled solder or sinter interfaces. X-ray inspection is used where required to verify joint quality and voiding.</p></div></div></div><div style="margin-top:22px; padding-top:18px; border-top:1px solid var(--line);"><a href="/markets/automotive" style="font-size:12px; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:0.07em; text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--hana-blue); text-decoration:none; display:inline-flex; align-items:center; gap:6px; white-space:nowrap; line-height:1.4;"><i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:13px;height:13px;"></i> Back to the Automotive market hub</a></div></div></div><section class="auto-cta auto-cta--spoke" style="background:var(--hana-blue-deep);" data-hana-bg="flow" data-variant="dark" data-accent="cyan" data-fade="none"><div class="inner"><div><h2>Have a power-module program in mind?</h2><p>Send a device spec and target volumes. We'll come back with a DFM read, a thermal-path view, and an indicative plan.</p></div><div class="actions"><a href="/contact" class="auto-btn auto-btn--ondark-primary">Start a program <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:13px;height:13px;"></i></a></div></div></section></main></div></div>

